==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tubbe}}, {{m|enm|tobbe}}, from {{der|en|dum|tubbe}} or {{der|en|gml|tubbe}}, {{m|gml|tobbe}}, further etymology unknown. Considered to be unrelated to {{m|en|tube}}<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|tŭb}}, {{IPA|en|/tʌb/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-tub.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌb|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Tub of cottage cheese.jpg|thumb|Tub of cottage cheese, lid, and lidding film]]

# A [[flat]]-[[bottomed]] [[vessel]], of width similar to or greater than its height, used for [[storing]] or [[packing]] things, or for [[washing]] things in.
#: {{ux|en|He bought a '''tub''' of lard to roast the potatoes in.}}
# The [[content]]s or [[capacity]] of such a vessel.
#: {{ux|en|She added a '''tub''' of margarine to the stew.}}
# A [[bathtub]].
#* '''1920''', Theodore Sharpe, ''My Place in the Shade: And Various Verse'' (page 27)
#*: Teach me to love my morning '''tub''', / In waters cold to splash and rub; / O, grant my Turkish towel may flood / Its virtues through my soul and blood.
# {{lb|en|nautical|informal}} A [[slow]]-[[moving]] [[craft]].
# {{lb|en|humorous|or|derogatory}} Any structure shaped like a tub, such as a certain old form of [[pulpit]], a short broad [[boat]], etc.
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=All being took up and busied, some in pulpits and some in '''tubs''', in the grand work of preaching and holding forth.}}
# A small [[cask]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''tub''' of gin}}
# Any of various historically designated quantities of goods to be sold by the tub (butter, oysters, etc).
# {{lb|en|mining}} A box or bucket in which [[coal]] or [[ore]] is sent up a [[shaft]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[sweat]]ing in a tub; a [[tub fast]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|4|3|passage='''tubs''' and baths; bring down rose-cheeked youth <br>To the tub-fast and the diet}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A corpulent or obese person.
#* '''2003''', Trey Ellis, ''Platitudes: & the New Black Aesthetic'' (page 139)
#*: Donald tells him to be more realistic. Take those two girls over there, for example. One's a zitface and the other's a '''tub''', so they'd be perfect for them.

